  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>3f6ebdd7298bf252ed64986754d4ec4a</srcmd5>
    <version>3.3.0</version>
    <time>1787656801</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-blobfile from 3.0.0 to 3.3.0 (upstream 2026-08-20), folding in
the 3.1.0 and 3.2.0 releases.

3.3.0: streaming writes in the higher level APIs; fix partial_writes_on_exc=False
being ignored when a write to an Azure file failed while being prepared; clean up
the accessTokens.json code path.

3.2.0: new partial_writes_on_exc argument on BlobFile; write_text/write_bytes/copy
avoid partial remote writes when interrupted; new BLOBFILE_REDIRECT_RETRY_COUNT
environment variable; error out when a local path looks like a URL; requires
urllib3 &gt;= 2 and Python &gt;= 3.10.

3.1.0: improved bf.join, optional blind writes, EAI_NODATA handled like
EAI_NONAME in the DNS retry logic.

Packaging: the urllib3 floor moves from 1.25.3 to 2 and the setuptools build
requirement from 64.0 to 69, both as demanded by upstream metadata. The CRLF
conversion of README.md and LICENSE is dropped since upstream now ships them
with LF line endings.

Built for openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64: green, rpmlint 0 errors, 0 warnings,
0 badness; the self-contained XML parser tests pass on both python313 and
python314. No patches carried.</comment>
    <requestid>1373465</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
